  "user_request_original": "Design a 27-layer defective DBR bandpass filter on Fused Silica substrate with Air incident medium using Ta2O5 (high index) and SiO2 (low index). Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5 (cavity), SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2. Initialize thicknesses using linear chirp: layer k thickness = quarter_wave_1550nm * (0.8 + 0.4*(k-1)/26) where quarter_wave_1550nm for Ta2O5 is lambda0/(4*n_Ta2O5) and for SiO2 is lambda0/(4*n_SiO2), cavity layer (layer 15, Ta2O5) initialized at half-wave optical thickness. Optimize all 27 thicknesses with bounds 50-350 nm for mirror layers, 400-700 nm for cavity. Evaluate coherent TMM transmittance at normal incidence, unpolarized. Target wavelengths: maximize at 1550 nm, suppress in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands. Topology realization override: disregard any symbolic repeat count, range, or ellipsis above and use exactly 5 alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 pairs, one cavity layer, and exactly 5 reverse-order pairs (21 finite layers). Optimize only continuous physical thicknesses; the task compiler must fully expand every finite layer. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 1400-1500 nm, 1550-1550 nm, 1600-1700 nm. soft objectives: high transmittance at 1550 nm (soft target ≥ 0.95); strong suppression of transmittance in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: transmittance in 1400-1500 nm; transmittance in 1600-1700 nm. manufacturing constraints: total layers ≤ 30.",
  "normalized_request_english": "Design a 21-layer defective DBR bandpass filter on fused silica with air incidence using Ta2O5 and SiO2. Sequence: five alternating Ta/Si pairs, one central Ta cavity layer, five additional alternating pairs. Initialize mirror layers near quarter-wave thickness at 1550 nm, cavity near half-wave. Optimize all 21 thicknesses (mirrors 50-350 nm, cavity 400-700 nm) using coherent TMM at normal incidence, unpolarized. Maximize transmission at 1550 nm while minimizing transmission in 1400-1500 nm and 1600-1700 nm bands.",
